A||||4||BobC||Anyone know where to find production numbers for 87 & 88?
Z||000000||BobC||08-24-99||07:38 AM||||I'm interested in the GT's, Formula's and maybe SE's.  A breakdown by color is what I'm looking for.  The ones I like are Silver, Gold, White, Yellow and Blue.  A link or info would be appreciated.<p>BobC
Z||000001||87GT||08-24-99||09:08 PM||||In 1987, there were 46,529 fieros built.  There were 8,402 in Black.  4,458 in Blue.  2 in Bright Red.  4,119 in Lt Gold Metallic.  20,264 in Medium Red Met.  6,671 in Silver.  2,611 in White.  In 87, there were 15,968 GTs built.  3,135 Sports.  3,875 SEs.  and 23,603 Base fieros.   NOW FOR 88.  In 1988, there were 26,401 fieros built.  There were 4,602 in black.  10,238 in Bright Red.  2,729 in Medium Red Met.  1,256 in Silver.  6,404 in White.  1,166 in Yellow.  in 88, there were 6,848 GTs built.  and 19,553 base fieros made.  It doesnt say on my list how many formulas were made though.  If have any other questions, let me know
Z||000002||batboy||08-25-99||07:51 PM||||Here's an address to check out on-line for Fiero color and production numbers:<p>http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/Fieroproduction.htm
Z||000003||BobC||08-25-99||09:46 PM||||Thanks for the numbers, guys <IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15>
